   "text": "Modernhard-drivesareveryfarfromtheselimits.A2015-eralaptopSSDweighs100grams,has an area of 100cm2 and stores 1TB = 8 × 1012 useful classical bits. This is a factor of 1028 below the 1041 qubits of the Bekenstein bound, and a factor of 1054 below the 1067 qubits of the holographic bound. Moore’s “law” predicts we will run up against the fundamental limits at the start of the twenty-third century.",
